title A ratchet passes on a low number
prompt kg -- take the refusal reflex across every scan
think Measured the surface before sweeping it, and the measurement changed the whole shape of the lap. The broad signature -- any instrument with || true -- matched 20 sites across 9 files. Reading each rather than fixing all of them: exactly 2 were faults. grep exits 1 when it finds nothing, so grep p f > out || true is right; an awk carrying END exit not-found is a PREDICATE whose non-zero is its answer. A meter with ninety percent false positives is a meter somebody turns off.
obs The 26 Rishi true_witnesses that invoke a tracked awk by literal path already honor the reflex -- assert awk.ok else with a named message. Counting them as faults would have been wrong, and I nearly did before checking one.
think The two real faults sit in unheard_guard_scan.sh, and they fail differently. The first feeds a transitive closure, so an empty result stops the walk early, unheard reads high, and the ceiling reds -- loud, and wrong in the safe direction. The second feeds choirs, and a ratchet passes on a LOW number: an empty result reads unheard_choirs=0 against a ceiling of 37, the greenest number on the page.
obs That is the lesson worth carrying past this file. A gate at zero fails SAFE when its instrument dies -- no evidence, no pass. A ceiling fails UNSAFE -- no evidence reads as nothing wrong. This tree holds far more ceilings than gates, so the failure mode of a dead instrument is systematically toward false comfort.
obs The meter's own first run found a third site I had not, counsel_census_scan.sh, and it turned out to be a documented deliberate toleration: one dangling symlink among six thousand paths fails the cat, and the fifty-six megabytes that DID read are the census. A decision, not a swallow -- and the difference between them is whether anyone wrote it down. So a # instrument-tolerated: comment exempts the next line and nothing else, which puts the exemption one line from the thing it exempts and makes it carry its reason.
obs The meter failed its own law on the first draft: pointed at a root it could not reach, it emitted a bare shell cd error rather than instrument=failed. The control asserted that leg and caught it. A rule its own instrument does not follow is advice.
obs Gated at zero from birth rather than ratcheted down, because both known faults were repaired on the lap the meter was written. There was nothing to grandfather.
loom guard=instrument_refusal scans_read=676 swallowed=0 ceiling=0 pen_legs=11 wall_s=1
loom signature broad_matches=20 real_faults=2 tolerations_documented=1
file tools/fixtures/u/unheard_guard_scan.sh both awk passes check their status and refuse naming the instrument, with awk's own last five lines
file tools/fixtures/i/instrument_refusal_scan.sh the narrow reading, gated at zero, obeying the law it enforces
file tools/fixtures/i/instrument_refusal_control.sh eleven behaviors, every refusal from both sides and every welcome asserted as hard
file tools/i/instrument_refusal_witness.rish the guard, rostered at tier lap the lap it was written
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- his mid-turn correction stands next: the microkernel vision is intrinsically non-POSIX, which is a framing error in the yonder study I shipped, and the permissive musl/Rust/Zig implementations want their own research pass
